  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Deloitte Consulting obligated $1.8B in FY2026 to date. Deloitte Consulting received 502 awards so far, with an average award size of $3.7M, and obligations fell 38.3% year over year. Deloitte Consulting obligations trended upward from FY21 through FY24: FY21 was $2.4B, FY22 was $2.6B, FY23 was $2.9B, and FY24 peaked at $3.3B, then declined to $3B in FY25 and to $1.8B in FY26. The General Services Administration is the largest buying agency in FY2026 to date at $493M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $311M and the Department of Defense at $292M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $869M, followed by Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $422M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $194M. These figures are contract obligations except where noted as total contract values in award-value tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which federal agencies are the biggest buyers of Deloitte Consulting in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration bought $493M. The Department of Veterans Affairs bought $311M and the Department of Defense bought $292M. The Department of Health and Human Services bought $251M, and the Department of Homeland Security bought $165M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services drive Deloitte Consulting's federal obligations?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services drove the largest share at $869M. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services contributed $422M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences contributed $194M. Engineering Services accounted for $191M, with smaller contributions across other professional and technical service categories."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Deloitte Consulting make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Deloitte Consulting obligated $1.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Deloitte Consulting received 502 awards so far, with an average award size of $3.7M, and obligations fell 38.3% year over year. Historical obligations were $2.4B in FY21, $2.6B in FY22, $2.9B in FY23, $3.3B in FY24, and $3B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Deloitte Consulting?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration, the Department of Veterans Affairs, and the Department of Defense are the top buyers. The General Services Administration bought $493M, the Department of Veterans Affairs bought $311M, and the Department of Defense bought $292M in FY2026 to date. Other notable buying agencies include the Department of Health and Human Services at $251M and the Department of Homeland Security at $165M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Deloitte Consulting sell to the government?",
      "a": "Deloitte Consulting sells primarily Computer Systems Design Services and management consulting to the government. Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $869M, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounted for $422M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $194M in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services accounted for $191M and other professional services made up additional smaller shares."
    },
